- The integer array parameter `nums` is sorted in non-decreasing order.
- If the integer parameter `target` is found in the integer array parameter `nums`, the integer array result contains the starting and ending positions of the integer parameter `target`.
- If the integer parameter `target` is not found in the integer array parameter `nums`, the integer array result is [-1, -1].
- The integer array result has a length of 2.
- The runtime complexity of the algorithm is O(log n).